## The two fixes

1. B1 on step D6. The song player in class-screen mode was 1770 px tall: the 16:9 stage 530 px
   plus an unbounded 15-line lyric list of 1072 px. `song.tsx` now marks the class-screen mode on
   the stage, and `globals.css` adds two rules for that mode only: the stage caps at 44 percent
   of the screen height, and the lyric list bounds at 25 percent and scrolls inside its box.
   Only the class-screen mode changes; the at-home layout and its Phase 3 tests stay the same.
   Result: `player_h=913` at 1920x1080, `player_h=698` at 1366x768, both fit.
2. L4. The `Play clip` control was 83x34 px. `ClipControl` in `lesson-flow.tsx` now holds
   `min-h-[44px] min-w-[44px]` with centered content. The gate measures `min_side_px=44` over 13
   targets (12 drill, 1 recall).

